    {
      "name": "eased_then_linear_three_keys",
      "comment": "red -> green -> blue over [0, 1 s, 2 s]. The FIRST segment is the CSS ease_in_out cubic (out = (0.42, 0), in = (0.58, 1)); the second is Linear. That cubic is point-symmetric about (0.5, 0.5), so its eased progress at the segment's midpoint is exactly 0.5 -- which is why t = 0.5 s expects the SAME red/green OkLab midpoint the linear `red_to_green` case carries, and needs no new external anchor. The three key times pin the endpoints, where a segment class must never move the value.",
